{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"DOI:\"10.1126/science.7678183\"","resultType":"core","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":5,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"7678183","source":"MED","pmid":"7678183","doi":"10.1126/science.7678183","title":"Adipose expression of tumor necrosis factor-alpha: direct role in obesity-linked insulin resistance.","authorString":"Hotamisligil GS, Shargill NS, Spiegelman BM.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Hotamisligil GS","lastName":"Hotamisligil","firstName":"G S","initials":"GS","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Dana-Farber Cancer Institute, Boston, MA."}]}},{"fullName":"Shargill NS","lastName":"Shargill","firstName":"N S","initials":"NS"},{"fullName":"Spiegelman BM","lastName":"Spiegelman","firstName":"B M","initials":"BM"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","wikipedia"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"5091","volume":"259","journalIssueId":651677,"dateOfPublication":"1993 Jan","monthOfPublication":1,"yearOfPublication":1993,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Science","title":"Science (New York, N.Y.)","essn":"1095-9203","issn":"0036-8075","isoabbreviation":"Science","nlmid":"0404511"},"printPublicationDate":"1993-01-01"},"pubYear":"1993","pageInfo":"87-91","abstractText":"Tumor necrosis factor-alpha (TNF-alpha) has been shown to have certain catabolic effects on fat cells and whole animals. An induction of TNF-alpha messenger RNA expression was observed in adipose tissue from four different rodent models of obesity and diabetes. TNF-alpha protein was also elevated locally and systemically. Neutralization of TNF-alpha in obese fa/fa rats caused a significant increase in the peripheral uptake of glucose in response to insulin. These results indicate a role for TNF-alpha in obesity and particularly in the insulin resistance and diabetes that often accompany obesity.","affiliation":"Dana-Farber Cancer Institute, Boston, MA.","publicationStatus":"ppublish